n't matter. n4 removable, symbol s1? Wait n4 symbol is 's1' which is required! So cannot remove because symbol is in required_symbols. So n4 stays. n5 not removable. n6 removable, symbol s0 not required, children none -> remove n6. Then depth1 nodes: n1, n2, n3. Order ids: n1, n2, n3. n1 not removable, n2 removable, n2's children: n4 (retained because not removed), so has retained child -> cannot remove n2. n3 not removable. So only n6 removed. So final retained: all except n6. That seems plausible.\n\nOur algorithm would process depth descending: n4 (depth2), but n4 symbol 's1' is required, skip. n5 not removable, skip. n6 removal proceeds. Then depth1: n1 not removable, n2 removable but children n4 retained -> skip, n3 not removable. So removed_order = [\"n6\"], retained = sorted ids of all except n6: [\"n1\",\"n2\",\"n3\",\"n4\",\"n5\",\"root\"] sorted lexicographically: [\"n1\",\"n2\",\"n3\",\"n4\",\"n5\",\"root\"].\n\nThat matches our reasoning.\n\nNow, we need to output as JSON string inside \"implementation\". Also need to handle escaping. We'll write the function as a string.\n\nBut note: The instruction says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\" So we do that.\n\nAlso \"Use only quantities present in the case payload. Do not call a language model, network service, random generator, wall clock, or environment-dependent resource.\" We abide.\n\nNow produce final answer.\n\nThe response must be exactly one valid JSON object with key \"implementation\". No markdown. We'll format the Python code string with proper escaping.\n\nWe can use triple quotes inside the string, but JSON requires escaping newlines and quotes. We'll write as a single line, but it's easier to write the code with actual newlines and then escape them. Since we are writing the JSON manually, we can use a tool or careful escaping. We'll produce the JSON string.\n\nLet's produce the Python code as a string with escaped newline char