    nid = n['id']\\n            if nid in removed_set or nid == exclude_id:\\n                continue\\n            present.add(n['symbol'])\\n        return all(sym in present for sym in required_symbols)\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node['id']\\n        if not node['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if nid == 'root':\\n            continue\\n        if node['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        children = parent_to_children.get(nid, [])\\n        has_retained_children = any(cid not in removed_set for cid in children)\\n        if has_retained_children:\\n            continue\\n        if required_symbols_retained(exclude_id=nid):\\n            removed_set.add(nid)\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n    retained_node_ids = sorted([n['id'] for n in nodes if n['id'] not in removed_set])\\n    return {\\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order, \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_node_ids}\"}\n```\n\nBut note: In the code, we used `node.get('removable')` which is a bool from JSON. But JSON booleans are lowercase true/false, Python sees them as True/False. Fine.\n\nAlso need to ensure that the depth field is present, we used node['depth'] in key. That's fine.\n\nOne more thing: The instruction says \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" We already check root via nid == 'root'. Also we check required symbol. And we check retained children.\n\nBut there is also \"Never remove ... a required symbol\" - we check symbol in required_symbols. But what if a node's symbol is required but it is removable? We skip. Good.\n\nAlso \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" That is our check.\n\nWe didn't consider utility field at all. The description mentions \"utility\" but no rule about using it. So we ignore it.\n\nNow final output."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2172,"completion_tokens":4980,"total_tokens